<?phem

namespace App\Ui\Demos;

use Phem\Attribute\{Component, Page, State};
use Phem\{Event, Node, Reply, ToastType};

use function App\Ui\{DemoPage, Example, Examples, Hero};
use function Phem\Ui\Base\{ToastClose, ToastContent, ToastData, ToastDescription, ToastRoot, ToastTitle};
use Phem\Ui\Base\{Button, ToastViewport};

#[Page('/components/toast')]
function ToastPage(): Node
{
    return (
        <DemoPage slug="toast">
            <Hero source="ToastHeroDemo">
                <ToastHeroDemo />
            </Hero>
            <Examples>
                <Example title="Anchored toasts" source="ToastAnchoredDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Toasts can be anchored to a specific element: give the toast the <code>anchor</code> option with the <code>id</code> of the element. This is useful for showing contextual feedback like transient "Copied" toasts that appear near the button that triggered the action.</p>
                        <p>Anchored toasts should be rendered in a separate <code>ToastViewport</code> from stacked toasts: an <code>anchored</code> viewport with a <code>name</code>, and the <code>viewport</code> option of the toast. The anchored viewport places each toast on its <code>side</code>, with its <code>sideOffset</code>.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ToastAnchoredDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Custom position" source="ToastPositionDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>The position of the toasts is controlled by the <code>position</code> prop of <code>ToastViewport</code>: <code>bottom-right</code> (the default) or <code>top-center</code>. A toast at the top closes with a swipe up. The following shows a top-center position.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ToastPositionDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Undo action" source="ToastUndoDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>When adding a toast, the <code>action</code> option gives the label of an action button inside of it. A click on the button closes the toast and calls the <code>onCall</code> handler of the viewport, with the <code>action</code>, the <code>id</code> and the <code>data</code> of the toast in <code>$e-&gt;detail</code>: this enables the ability to undo an action associated with the toast.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ToastUndoDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Promise" source="ToastPromiseDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>An asynchronous toast can be created with three possible states: <code>loading</code>, <code>success</code>, and <code>error</code>. The <code>type</code> string matches these states to change the styling.</p>
                        <p>Here, the button has <code>data-phem-toast-show</code> with the detail of a <code>loading</code> toast: it shows at the click, before the server answers. The handler answers after two seconds with a <code>success</code> or an <code>error</code> toast with the same <code>id</code>, which updates the loading toast.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ToastPromiseDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Custom" source="ToastCustomDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>A toast with custom data can be created by passing an array to the <code>data</code> option. Each <code>ToastData</code> part of the template of the viewport shows the value of its <code>name</code>.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ToastCustomDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Deduplicated toast" source="ToastDeduplicatedDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>When you show the same toast by <code>id</code>, the toast on the screen updates, and its <code>data-update-key</code> attribute counts the updates. Its <code>data-updated</code> attribute comes again with each update, so a CSS animation on <code>[data-updated]</code> plays again while the same toast stays on the screen.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ToastDeduplicatedDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Varying heights" source="ToastVaryingHeightsDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>Toasts with varying heights are stacked by clamping every toast's height to the frontmost toast at index 0 using the <code>--toast-frontmost-height</code> CSS variable, while the <code>data-behind</code> attribute hides the content of the toasts behind it. Avoid sizing <code>ToastContent</code> to the root's height (such as <code>height: 100%</code>), as resizing it alongside the root cancels the root's height transition.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <ToastVaryingHeightsDemo />
                </Example>
            </Examples>
        </DemoPage>
    );
}

// The viewport with no name shows the toasts with no `viewport` option: the toasts of
// the other examples also show in it.
#[Component]
final class ToastHeroDemo
{
    #[State] public int $count = 0;

    public function create(Reply $reply): void
    {
        ++$this->count;
        $reply->toast(
            'This is a toast notification.',
            title: 'Toast '.$this->count.' created',
        );
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <div className="contents">
                <Button onClick={{ create }}>Create toast</Button>
                <ToastViewport />
            </div>
        );
    }
}

// The click copies the text and shows the toast in the browser: no server event. While the toast
// shows, the button has `data-copied`: its check icon, and the look of a disabled button.
#[Component]
function ToastAnchoredDemo(): Node
{
    $toast = json_encode([
        'message' => 'Copied',
        'duration' => 1500,
        'anchor' => 'toast-copy',
        'viewport' => 'anchored',
    ]);

    return (
        <div className="contents">
            <Button
                id="toast-copy"
                aria-label="Copy to clipboard"
                data-controller="phem-clipboard"
                data-phem-clipboard-text-value="composer require phem/ui-base"
                data-phem-clipboard-duration-value={{ 1500 }}
                data-action="phem-clipboard#copy"
                data-phem-toast-show={{ toast }}
                className="group w-8 px-0 data-copied:pointer-events-none data-copied:border-neutral-500 data-copied:text-neutral-500 dark:data-copied:border-neutral-400 dark:data-copied:text-neutral-400"
            >
                <svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" className="block group-data-copied:hidden">
                    <rect width="8" height="4" x="8" y="2" rx="1" ry="1" />
                    <path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2" />
                </svg>
                <svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" className="hidden group-data-copied:block">
                    <path d="m2.5 8.5 4 4 7-9" />
                </svg>
            </Button>
            <ToastViewport name="anchored" anchored sideOffset={{ 10 }} />
        </div>
    );
}

#[Component]
final class ToastPositionDemo
{
    #[State] public int $count = 0;

    /** A toast at the top of the screen. */
    public function create(Reply $reply): void
    {
        ++$this->count;
        $reply->toast(
            'This is a toast notification.',
            title: 'Toast '.$this->count.' created',
            viewport: 'top',
        );
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <div className="contents">
                <Button onClick={{ create }}>Create toast</Button>
                <ToastViewport name="top" position="top-center" />
            </div>
        );
    }
}

#[Component]
final class ToastUndoDemo
{
    /** A toast with an action button. */
    public function perform(Reply $reply): void
    {
        $reply->toast(
            'You can undo this action.',
            ToastType::Success,
            10000,
            'Action performed',
            action: 'Undo',
            viewport: 'undo',
        );
    }

    /** The action button of a toast calls the `onCall` handler of the viewport. */
    public function undo(Event $e, Reply $reply): void
    {
        if ('Undo' === ($e->detail['action'] ?? null)) {
            $reply->toast('Action undone', viewport: 'undo');
        }
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <div className="contents">
                <Button onClick={{ perform }}>Perform action</Button>
                <ToastViewport name="undo" onCall={{ undo }} />
            </div>
        );
    }
}

// The toasts show in the viewport with no name, in the hero.
#[Component]
final class ToastPromiseDemo
{
    #[State] public int $promises = 0;

    /** The loading toast of the click becomes the toast of the answer. */
    public function run(Reply $reply): void
    {
        $id = 'promise-'.++$this->promises;

        // Simulate an API request that ends after 2 seconds.
        usleep(2_000_000);

        if (random_int(1, 10) <= 7) {
            $reply->toast('Success: operation completed', ToastType::Success, id: $id);
        } else {
            $reply->toast('Error: operation failed', ToastType::Error, id: $id);
        }
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        $loading = json_encode([
            'message' => 'Loading data…',
            'type' => 'loading',
            'id' => 'promise-'.($this->promises + 1),
            'duration' => 0,
        ]);

        return (
            <Button onClick={{ run }} data-phem-toast-show={{ loading }}>Run promise</Button>
        );
    }
}

#[Component]
final class ToastCustomDemo
{
    /** A toast with data for the template. */
    public function create(Reply $reply): void
    {
        $reply->toast(
            'Toast with custom data',
            data: ['userId' => '123'],
            viewport: 'custom',
        );
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <div className="contents">
                <Button onClick={{ create }}>Create custom toast</Button>
                <ToastViewport name="custom">
                    <ToastRoot>
                        <ToastContent>
                            <div className="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-1">
                                <ToastDescription className="font-bold" />
                                <p className="text-sm">data.userId is <ToastData name="userId" /></p>
                            </div>
                            <ToastClose>Dismiss</ToastClose>
                        </ToastContent>
                    </ToastRoot>
                </ToastViewport>
            </div>
        );
    }
}

#[Component]
final class ToastDeduplicatedDemo
{
    /** The same id updates the toast on the screen. */
    public function save(Reply $reply): void
    {
        $reply->toast(
            'Click again while it is visible to replay the pulse.',
            title: 'Draft saved',
            id: 'save-status',
            viewport: 'pulse',
        );
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <div className="contents">
                <Button onClick={{ save }}>Save draft</Button>
                <ToastViewport name="pulse">
                    <ToastRoot className="data-updated:animate-[toast-pulse_0.28s_ease]">
                        <ToastContent>
                            <div className="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-1">
                                <ToastTitle />
                                <ToastDescription />
                            </div>
                            <ToastClose>Dismiss</ToastClose>
                        </ToastContent>
                    </ToastRoot>
                </ToastViewport>
            </div>
        );
    }
}

// The toasts show in the viewport with no name, in the hero.
#[Component]
final class ToastVaryingHeightsDemo
{
    private const array TEXTS = [
        'Short message.',
        'A bit longer message that spans two lines.',
        'This is a longer description that intentionally takes more vertical space to demonstrate stacking with varying heights.',
        'An even longer description that should span multiple lines so we can verify the clamped collapsed height and smooth expansion animation when hovering or focusing the viewport.',
    ];

    #[State] public int $count = 0;

    public function create(Reply $reply): void
    {
        ++$this->count;
        $reply->toast(
            self::TEXTS[random_int(0, \count(self::TEXTS) - 1)],
            title: 'Toast '.$this->count.' created',
        );
    }

    public function render(): Node
    {
        return (
            <Button onClick={{ create }}>Create varying height toast</Button>
        );
    }
}
